### Member Registration API — the two calls Descope's flow connectors make.
### The caller is the Descope engine, server to server, authenticated with the connector key.
### Run the API in Development (InMemory DB + the dev connector key) and send these in order.

@host = https://localhost:7001
@connectorKey = dev-connector-key
@email = jane.member@example.com

### Step 1 — Descope has verified the email; store the details and get the pending record's id.
# Copy `userId` from the response into @userId below.
POST {{host}}/api/initiateRegistration
Content-Type: application/json
X-Connector-Key: {{connectorKey}}

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Member",
  "dateOfBirth": "1985-04-23",
  "zipCode": "12345",
  "contactNumber": "123-456-7890"
}

### ^ paste the returned userId here
@userId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Step 2 — set the password and create the account.
POST {{host}}/api/registration/password
Content-Type: application/json
X-Connector-Key: {{connectorKey}}

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "password": "Str0ng!PassPhrase",
  "confirmPassword": "Str0ng!PassPhrase"
}

### Resuming — sending step 1 again for the same email returns the SAME userId, not a duplicate error.
POST {{host}}/api/initiateRegistration
Content-Type: application/json
X-Connector-Key: {{connectorKey}}

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Member",
  "dateOfBirth": "1985-04-23",
  "zipCode": "12345",
  "contactNumber": null
}

### Too-short password — expect 400 with the policy message.
POST {{host}}/api/registration/password
Content-Type: application/json
X-Connector-Key: {{connectorKey}}

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "password": "Short1!",
  "confirmPassword": "Short1!"
}

### No connector key — expect 401.
POST {{host}}/api/initiateRegistration
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nokey@example.com",
  "firstName": "No",
  "lastName": "Key",
  "dateOfBirth": "1985-04-23",
  "zipCode": "12345"
}

### Health
GET {{host}}/health
